{
  "_comment": "Flask HTML routes not reachable through the Cloudflare routing tables, measured 2026-09-05 against dchub-frontend@dbce499a8 (_routes.json 97/98 rules) and this repo at the commit that introduced the file. RATCHET: scripts/check_route_table_coherence.py fails on any NEW entry, so these lists may SHRINK BUT NEVER GROW. Nothing here is fixed by the commit that added it \u2014 the entries are recorded so that new mis-registration is visible. TWO LISTS, because the two tables fail differently and a path must not be allowed to migrate silently between them: missing_routes_json means the worker is NEVER INVOKED (404, or a same-named static file answers with NO x-dc-worker-version header \u2014 read that header PER PATH); missing_worker means the worker runs and declines to forward (403). THIS IS A DEBT REGISTER, NOT AN ALLOW-LIST. When a route here becomes covered the checker prints a ::notice:: naming it and you delete the line; that is how a payment gets recorded. Do NOT add an entry to silence a route you just broke \u2014 the fix is normally an entry in _routes.json 'include', and the cap is 98 rules counting include AND exclude together, currently 97/98, with rule 99 dropped SILENTLY (run `node scripts/check-edge-caps.mjs` in dchub-frontend; the cap is not stated anywhere in the file). Roughly 30 of these are known-dead or deliberately static: six 'static twins' (/cited-by, /system-status, /competitive, /watchlist, /feedback, /tax-incentives) where a static file is the correct thing to serve, four of whose handler files also serve the live /api/v1/* endpoints those pages call \u2014 deleting them would break the pages they appear to shadow. This register does NOT authorise deleting anything; its job is preventing NEW mis-registration. TO RE-MEASURE after a legitimate change: run the three phases (`python3 scripts/check_route_table_coherence.py flask-routes|route-tables|diff`) with a current dchub-frontend checkout and move only the lines the diff names. There is deliberately no --write-baseline flag: a guard that can bless itself is not a guard.",
